    {
      "id": "1e5e414c-9966-4f63-94b7-8f8ef4528d82",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## 08-15-02 daily restaurant prep list with AI\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Every morning the workflow reads the prep master list (menu items, stations, par levels) from Google Sheets.\n2. An AI agent plans what to prep today based on par levels and the day of the week, and returns the prep list with quantities.\n3. Each prep item is logged to the PrepLog sheet with a pending status so the kitchen can track progress.\n4. The prep list is sent to the kitchen on Telegram and emailed to the manager.\n5. The kitchen marks items done through the prep/complete webhook, which updates the log and confirms on Telegram.\n6. Every Monday a weekly report with completion rates is emailed and posted to Telegram.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Google Sheets, Gmail, Telegram, and OpenAI credentials.\n- Create a spreadsheet with a PrepItems sheet (item, station, par_qty, unit) and a PrepLog sheet (prep_date, row_key, item, station, qty, unit, status). Update the Google Sheets nodes with its ID.\n- Set the kitchen Telegram chat ID and the manager email in the notification nodes.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change the AI prompt, the daily schedule, or add more stations to match your kitchen."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
